1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,322
Orchard Core sends email for account confirmations, password resets, notifications, and workflows.

2
00:00:07,322 --> 00:00:11,943
Let's enable the SMTP provider, connect the site to a mail server, and

3
00:00:11,943 --> 00:00:14,800
send a test email to check that it works.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,583
Several parts of an Orchard Core site send email.

5
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:27,908
Users confirm their address and reset their password by email, notifications can reach

6
00:00:27,908 --> 00:00:32,480
an inbox, and a workflow can send a message with its Email Task activity.

7
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:38,827
The Email feature holds the settings, the Default provider, and the Email Test page.

8
00:00:38,827 --> 00:00:40,942
A provider does the sending:

9
00:00:40,942 --> 00:00:46,664
the SMTP Email Provider sends through an SMTP server, and Azure Communication Services

10
00:00:46,664 --> 00:00:49,960
Email, covered in a separate video, is another.

11
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:55,857
The Email settings and the Email Test page need the Manage Email Settings permission.

12
00:00:55,857 --> 00:00:59,760
The Administrator role has it, so the admin user can open both.

13
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:05,224
Let's enable the SMTP provider, configure it, and send a test email.

14
00:01:05,224 --> 00:01:11,020
A local test mail server shows the message arriving, so nothing reaches a real inbox.

15
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:18,511
Features are managed under Tools, Features.

16
00:01:18,511 --> 00:01:23,070
Let's open the Tools menu, choose Features, and search for SMTP.

17
00:01:26,099 --> 00:01:29,828
SMTP Email Provider is in the Communication category.

18
00:01:29,828 --> 00:01:35,769
It lists Email as a dependency, so enabling the provider also enables the Email feature.

19
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:37,763
Let's select Enable.

20
00:01:37,763 --> 00:01:42,040
A message confirms that the SMTP Email Provider feature was enabled.

21
00:01:42,601 --> 00:01:48,909
Searching for email lists the Email feature and the SMTP Email Provider, and both are enabled.

22
00:01:48,909 --> 00:01:52,631
Email adds the settings page and the Email Test page.

23
00:01:56,931 --> 00:02:00,637
The settings are under Settings, Communication, Email.

24
00:02:00,637 --> 00:02:05,951
The Providers tab opens first, with a warning that no email provider is enabled.

25
00:02:08,524 --> 00:02:12,513
The SMTP tab holds the settings of the SMTP provider.

26
00:02:12,513 --> 00:02:16,704
Let's check Enable SMTP Provider, and its fields appear.

27
00:02:17,162 --> 00:02:19,583
Sender email address is required.

28
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:24,424
It is the sender of every message, unless a message sets its own sender.

29
00:02:24,424 --> 00:02:26,782
Let's enter noreply@example.com.

30
00:02:27,245 --> 00:02:31,857
Delivery method is Network, which sends each message to a mail server.

31
00:02:31,857 --> 00:02:37,137
The other choice, Specified pickup directory, saves each message as a file, which

32
00:02:37,137 --> 00:02:39,625
helps while developing and testing.

33
00:02:40,122 --> 00:02:45,398
Under Network delivery options, Host name is the address of the SMTP server,

34
00:02:45,398 --> 00:02:48,486
and Port number is the port it listens on.

35
00:02:48,486 --> 00:02:51,832
The test server is on localhost, at port 2525.

36
00:02:52,288 --> 00:02:56,610
Encryption method to use offers None, SSL/TLS, and STARTTLS.

37
00:02:56,610 --> 00:03:01,193
The test server accepts plain connections, so let's choose None.

38
00:03:01,193 --> 00:03:06,038
Auto Select Encryption method would choose it from the port instead.

39
00:03:06,515 --> 00:03:11,427
Require credentials adds the Use Windows authentication option, and the User name and

40
00:03:11,427 --> 00:03:14,557
Password fields, for servers that ask for a sign-in.

41
00:03:14,557 --> 00:03:17,795
The test server does not, so let's leave it unchecked.

42
00:03:21,317 --> 00:03:22,706
Let's select Save.

43
00:03:22,706 --> 00:03:27,628
The page reloads on the Providers tab, with a confirmation message, and Default

44
00:03:27,628 --> 00:03:30,987
provider shows Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP).

45
00:03:31,531 --> 00:03:36,107
Orchard Core selected it for us, because no default provider was set.

46
00:03:36,107 --> 00:03:41,231
With several providers, this list chooses which one sends messages by default.

47
00:03:45,531 --> 00:03:49,636
The Email Test page is under Tools, Testing, Email Test.

48
00:03:49,636 --> 00:03:53,211
Provider is already set to the default provider.

49
00:03:55,263 --> 00:03:59,651
In To, let's enter the recipient, jamie.chen@example.com.

50
00:03:59,651 --> 00:04:01,392
Sender is optional:

51
00:04:01,392 --> 00:04:07,453
when it is empty, the message uses the sender email address of the SMTP settings.

52
00:04:07,913 --> 00:04:11,259
Cc, Bcc, and Reply To are optional as well.

53
00:04:11,259 --> 00:04:15,903
Subject and Body are required, so let's write a short message.

54
00:04:21,383 --> 00:04:22,671
Let's select Send.

55
00:04:22,671 --> 00:04:25,355
The page confirms the result with a message:

56
00:04:25,355 --> 00:04:27,073
Message sent successfully.

57
00:04:31,321 --> 00:04:34,359
Let's switch to the inbox of the test mail server.

58
00:04:34,359 --> 00:04:39,241
It lists the message the site sent, with the sender, the recipient, and the subject.

59
00:04:39,825 --> 00:04:41,367
Let's open the message.

60
00:04:41,367 --> 00:04:45,356
The sender is the address from the SMTP settings, and the subject and

61
00:04:45,356 --> 00:04:48,175
the text are the ones from the Email Test page.

62
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:56,376
When a message cannot be sent, the Email Test page lists the error.

63
00:04:56,376 --> 00:05:01,145
Check the host name, the port number, the encryption method, the credentials, and

64
00:05:01,145 --> 00:05:03,995
the email addresses, then send the test again.

65
00:05:05,995 --> 00:05:10,434
Enable the SMTP Email Provider, configure your mail server, and check it with

66
00:05:10,434 --> 00:05:11,824
the Email Test page.

67
00:05:11,824 --> 00:05:13,215
Thanks for watching.

